    {
      "slug": "nativity-campin",
      "title": "Nativity (Campin)",
      "year": 1430,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/La_Nativit%C3%A9%2C_par_Robert_Campin.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 2140,
      "imageHeight": 2560,
      "story": "Nativity is a panel painting of c. 1420 by the Early Netherlandish painter Robert Campin, now in the Musée des Beaux-Arts de Dijon, France. As often, the moment shown is the Adoration of the Shepherds. Harshly realistic, the Child Jesus and his parents are shown in poverty, the figures crowded in a small structure, with broken-down walls, and a thatched roof with a hole, the single space shared with animals. In this Campin abandons the traditional narrative.",
      "facts": [],
